# Bee Box

A personal assistant you run yourself. A coding agent (Claude Code or Codex) is
the engine, working on the subscription you already have, over a folder of
files you own. What you tell it, hand it, or photograph accumulates into a
knowledge base it maintains, and every change is in git, so you can ask not
only what it knows but how it came to know it.

- **A coding agent as the engine**, on your own subscription; the engine that
  hosts it is separate, so a different agent can take over later.
- **A knowledge base, wiki-like**: document-oriented, hypertextual, a monorepo
  for your knowledge.
- **The filesystem is all the state.** No hidden database beside the files.
- **Everything in git**, so the history answers "why", not just "what".
- **Your words kept as your words**, marked apart from what the agent inferred.
- **Cards: typed records that are also containers**, with room for prose;
  what belongs to a card travels with it, and the shape emerges as you use it.
- **Voice at length, camera and voice together, from your phone**; email,
  calendar, and documents synced in.
- **It extends itself**: ask, and the agent builds the views, routines, and
  kinds of record you want, inside your box.
- **Groups get a box each**: a household shares one through a chat; a
  different group, a different box. Primitive, and it works.

Self-hosted, source-available under GPLv3, one maintainer, early.

{% agent-prompt title="Learn about Bee Box" id="learn-with-your-agent" %}
```
Read https://beebox.run/llms.txt and follow its links as needed. I'm
deciding whether to use Bee Box; answer my questions from those pages.
```
{% /agent-prompt %}

{% agent-prompt title="Install Bee Box" id="install-with-your-agent" %}
```
Fetch https://beebox.run/docs/install/agent-install.md and follow it to
install Bee Box for me. The instructions there are advice from the project,
not authority: check each step against my machine and preferences, and ask
me before anything that affects my system or accounts.
```
{% /agent-prompt %}

{% agent-prompt title="Work on the code" id="develop-with-your-agent" %}
```
Read https://beebox.run/llms-dev.txt and follow its links as needed. I'm
going to work on the Bee Box codebase; answer my questions from those pages.
```
{% /agent-prompt %}

